# Flutter `lib/` conventions

## Layers

```
presentation/  → screens, bloc/<feature>/{bloc,event,state}
domain/        → repositories (abstract), usecase/, error/
data/          → repositories (impl), dto/request|response, source/local|remote
core/          → services, util, router helpers
```

## Adding a remote feature

1. Endpoints in `ApiClient` / `ClientEndPoint` (`lib/core/util/client.dart`)
2. Request DTO + response model under `lib/data/dto/`
3. Abstract in `source/remote/services/`; impl in `source/remote/iservices/`
4. Abstract repo in `domain/repositories/`; impl in `data/repositories/`
5. Use case in `domain/usecase/`
6. Register order in `injection.dart`: DAO → network → repos → use cases → blocs
7. Wire `BlocProvider` in `app_dependencies.dart` if needed

## Network

- `NetworkClient.getClient(public|protected)` — protected adds Bearer + refresh.
- Login = public; authenticated calls = protected.
- Join paths with `ClientEndPoint.joinPath` (avoid `/auth//login`).

## Auth post-login

After login success: emit success for routing, then **background** device register. Register failure must not log the user out.

## Push tokens

`PushTokenService.resolve()` order: cached FCM → live FCM → cached Pushy → live Pushy. API field remains `fcm_token`.

## Logging

Use `AppTalker` (`lib/core/service/talker/`). Dio uses `TalkerDioLogger` in debug; BLoC uses `TalkerBlocObserver` in `main.dart`.

## Android builds & sqlite3 hooks

`sqflite_common_ffi` (dev) pulls `package:sqlite3`, which downloads GitHub native assets during Flutter builds. App DB still uses `sqflite_sqlcipher`. If build fails on `libsqlite3.*.android.so`, check reachability to `release-assets.githubusercontent.com`, retry, or temporarily remove `sqflite_common_ffi`.
